# Model Selection (Usage Savings Priority)

**Default:** Composer 2.5. **Escalate:** GPT 5.6 Terra only when scope clearly exceeds Composer limits or needs frontier depth.

Owner priority is **month-long quota survival** — stretch Composer 2.5 first; Terra is a **scarce reserve**, not the default for “anything non-trivial.”

## Decision rule (apply first)

```
Can Composer 2.5 finish in ONE approved turn with a tight plan?
  • ≤2 related files (e.g. `.gd` + `.tres`, or two touched functions in one file)
  • ≤60 lines changed total
  • No new subsystem / manager / sim resolution-order change
  • Not a full class, full phase, or whole Master Bible rollout
  → Composer 2.5

Otherwise
  → GPT 5.6 Terra (first message must include a tight numbered plan)
```

Composer 2.5 workflow limits live in `AGENTS.md` § Composer 2.5. This rule governs **which model to open the chat with**.

## Use Composer 2.5 (expanded — prefer this)

| Task | Why it saves usage |
|------|-------------------|
| Read-only Q&A, grep, audits, reviews | No edit risk, cheapest turns |
| Micro fix (≤5 lines, one file) | Default Composer scope |
| Small-medium fix (~6–30 lines, one file) | Surgical edit |
| **Medium one-file fix (~31–60 lines)** with approved plan | Still cheaper than Terra if scoped |
| **Two related files** (e.g. ability `.tres` + factory hook, rule + `AGENTS.md` pointer) with approved plan | Avoid Terra for routine pairs |
| `.tres` / enum / constant / data-only skill defs | Data path, no new global rules |
| **Single Master Bible skill/passive** when data + one small hook, ≤2 files, ≤60 lines | Not a full class rollout |
| Scoped bug fix in combat/preview/commit (≤2 files, plan in first message) | Try Composer before Terra |
| Apply exact doc/rule diff owner already wrote | No exploration |

## Use GPT 5.6 Terra (reserve — don’t default here)

| Situation | Why Terra |
|-----------|-----------|
| **3+ files** or **>60 lines** in one turn | Beyond relaxed Composer ceiling |
| **Full class** or **full phase milestone** (“implement Phase N”, whole promotion tree) | Bible + architecture depth |
| **New subsystem, manager, or sim resolution-order change** | Wrong layer for Composer |
| **Co-op networking** or broad determinism refactor | High blast radius |
| Composer already failed or looped twice on same scoped task | Escalate, don’t keep burning Composer turns |
| Owner explicitly requests Terra or frontier model | Owner override |

**Terra first message must include:** numbered steps, files/functions, acceptance criteria. No wandering.

## Honor & Iron quick map

| Work | Model |
|------|--------|
| Explain existing code, read-only audit | Composer 2.5 |
| Micro fix through medium one-file fix (≤60 lines) | Composer 2.5 |
| Two-file scoped fix (`.gd` + `.tres`, rule + doc) | Composer 2.5 |
| Single skill/passive (data + small hook, ≤2 files) | Composer 2.5 |
| Scoped preview/commit bug (≤2 files, clear plan) | Composer 2.5 first |
| Full class from Master Bible | GPT 5.6 Terra |
| 3+ files (e.g. shader + scene + toggle + controller) | GPT 5.6 Terra |
| New manager / subsystem / resolution order | GPT 5.6 Terra |
| “Implement Phase N” end-to-end | GPT 5.6 Terra |

## Usage traps (both models)

1. **Premature Terra** — opening Terra for a 15-line two-file fix burns monthly reserve; try Composer first.
2. **Composer proposal loops** — bundle scope in one approved plan; after **two** failed Composer attempts on same task → Terra.
3. **Subagents** — burn quota twice; avoid unless owner explicitly requests.
4. **Terra without a plan** — one expensive wandering turn costs more than Composer read-only + Terra implement.
5. **Fast mode** — never for Composer 2.5 (`AGENTS.md`).

## Agent behavior

- **Default recommendation:** Composer 2.5 unless the decision rule clearly points to Terra.
- At chat start, state model fit in one sentence; **bias toward Composer** when within relaxed limits.
- If Terra-tier work lands on Composer → **attempt only if owner approves scoped plan** within limits; otherwise recommend Terra once, don’t loop defer messages.
- Do not recommend frontier models (Gemini Pro / Sonnet) when Composer or Terra within scope suffices — frontier is **last resort** for month-long quota.
